sequenceDiagram
    title Diagram 3: Buffer full - master blocks until a worker frees a slot
    actor C as Clients (burst)
    participant M as Master thread
    participant B as Request buffer<br/>(capacity = B slots)
    participant W as Worker thread

    activate W
    Note over W: All workers are busy handling earlier requests
    C->>+M: many connections arrive at once
    loop for each new connection
        M->>B: lock(mutex)
        alt count < B
            M->>B: put(conn_fd), count++
            B--)W: signal(not_empty)
        else count == B (buffer full)
            M->>B: wait(not_full) - releases mutex and sleeps
            Note over M,B: Master stops calling accept().<br/>New clients wait in the kernel backlog.
            W->>W: finish current request
            W->>B: lock, get() next request, count--
            B--)M: signal(not_full)
            W->>B: unlock(mutex)
            B-->>M: wait() returns, mutex re-acquired
            M->>B: put(conn_fd), count++
        end
        M->>B: unlock(mutex)
    end
    deactivate M
    W->>W: handle the request it just took
    W->>C: response
    deactivate W
    Note over C,W: Waiting time in the buffer = t_dequeue - t_arrive.<br/>This queueing delay is what raises p99 latency under load.
